# Documentation

Document **what exists**. Never describe unbuilt behavior as live (E, C §9, D §7, hard-close HTTP, PDF export, company onboarding UI).

- Specs: standing rules in the body; decision log is append-only (do not silently rewrite D-1… or A #1…).
- Cite `[feature-spec.md §x]` / `[Rules §x]` in code comments for non-trivial logic.
- `schema.sql` comments are part of the schema SoT.
- After behavior changes, update the **module feature spec** if the rule changed; do not only edit the user manual.
- Known stale docs: `.cursor/references/source-of-truth.md`. Prefer the module spec + `schema.sql` when they disagree with README or `INFINITY_ACCOUNTING_DOCUMENTATION.md`.

Feature write-up: `.cursor/skills/document-feature/SKILL.md`. Drift check: `.cursor/workflows/documentation-drift.md`.